From c336b54ae14225d898fe80acc79ffa30d5b65c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:15:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Convert upstream's KEYS file (https://archive.apache.org/dist/ant/KEYS)
with GnuPG into KEYS.pgp, a plain OpenPGP keyring with every key GnuPG
reads from it (19); sqv cannot read the KEYS file itself: it holds 2 v3
(PGP 2) keys, which Sequoia does not parse, so sqv rejects the whole
file (GnuPG skips such keys silently). Its Source line names the new
file instead of https://archive.apache.org/dist/ant/KEYS, which is not
what the file holds any more.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore       |   1 -
 KEYS.pgp         | Bin 0 -> 53023 bytes
 ant-antunit.spec |   6 +++++-
 sources          |   1 -
 4 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 KEYS.pgp

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 2c4c95b..4fdf7e7 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -3,7 +3,6 @@
 /apache-ant-antunit-1.3-src.tar.bz2
 /apache-ant-antunit-1.4-src.tar.bz2
 /apache-ant-antunit-1.4.1-src.tar.bz2
-/KEYS
 /apache-ant-antunit-1.4.1-src.tar.bz2.asc
 /apache-ant-antunit-1.5.0-src.tar.bz2
 /apache-ant-antunit-1.5.0-src.tar.bz2.asc
diff --git a/KEYS.pgp b/KEYS.pgp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b2d4ba847eadf85d59aa666c1155e6e568f539a1
